title "The Legend of Zelda - Overworld"
description "Transcribed from the supplied z1overw.mid; MIDI arrangement credited to Jeffrey M Colletti. All four parts, original pitches, triplets, articulation, and tempo retained."

// Source: z1overw.mid, SMF format 1, 384 pulses per quarter note.
// MIDI tempo is exactly 405405 microseconds/quarter (approximately 148 BPM).
// 24 bars in 4/4, B-flat major; loop the complete supplied arrangement.
// Duration multipliers such as 8*2/3 are triplet eighths.
// Gate fractions preserve the MIDI note lengths, including its short gaps.
// Five overlapping same-pitch harmony notes retrigger on the newer onset.
// The final bass release is one 4ms tick early so it precedes the Loop event.
// GM snare 38 maps to B6 noise (a drum ID is not a pitched D2).
// Envelopes approximate NES timbres; the engine's channel encoding is unchanged.

tempo 4000000/27027
meter 4/4
loop
automation 8ms

envelope pulse {
    points 0ms:100%, 24ms:90%, 72ms:85%
    sustain
}
envelope triangle {
    points 0ms:100%, 32ms:90%
    sustain
}
envelope snare {
    points 0ms:100%, 8ms:75%, 36ms:30%, 76ms:0%
}
instrument lead { wave square volume 11 envelope pulse }
instrument harmony { wave square volume 8 envelope pulse }
instrument bass { wave triangle volume 10 envelope triangle }
instrument drum { wave noise volume 2 envelope snare }
